From acdbe07d8b0cf09a3cd43bf6ff655ddfecd8de90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:36:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Repair and finalize documentation

Fix structural and cross-document issues found in the documentation audit,
without inventing any academic data:

- Rename "Academic Planner" to "UnitControl" (File 01).
- Replace File 03 (previously the generation prompt) with the actual
  UX/UI specification.
- Clarify Major vs Orientation: Computer Engineering is the major;
  Software Engineering / Information Technology / Unified are orientations
  (Files 01, 04, 06).
- Reconcile Files 05 and 07: drop required_units and elective_group_id from
  the curriculum-course link, align course_groups on group_type, add a
  category field to curriculum_requirements, and make course_group_courses
  the single source of group membership.
- Model course attempt history (student_course_attempts) so retakes,
  "previously attempted" checks, and the failed-course recovery window can
  be represented; keep temporary PLANNED planning separate from persistent
  history; record semester GPA per term (Files 05, 07, 09).
- Document that the pre-1403 dataset defines two curricula (SE, IT) sharing
  common sections; mark the exact per-orientation composition as requiring
  verification (File 06).
- Flag the previously unacknowledged duplicate code 7000031588 and mark all
  duplicate-code / category conflicts as requiring official verification;
  preserve supplied data unchanged (Files 06, 10).
- Add Persian/RTL/i18n requirements implied by the dataset (Files 03, 09).
- Mark expired-failed-course blocking behavior and corequisite enforcement
  semantics as TBD pending verification (File 04).
- Remove the malformed outer code-fence wrapper that made 8 files render as
  raw code blocks.

Course data, credits, prerequisites, corequisites, credit limits, and
final-semester rules remain untouched and marked TBD.

